          "y": 16,
          "width": 96,
          "line_height": 9,
          "text": "ArrayAstBuilder starts from an outer circle and builds a GroupNode. Direct children become SymbolNodes or nested GroupNodes by role, allowing a finished child array to become input"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "modopedia:text",
      "x": 2,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 96,
      "line_height": 9,
      "text": "to a parent array."
    },
    {
      "type": "modopedia:text",
      "x": 2,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 96,
      "line_height": 9,
      "text": "$(f:minecraft:uniform)GroupNode(boundary)\n  └─ SequenceNode(children)\n       ├─ SymbolNode(parameter)\n       ├─ SymbolNode(center)\n       └─ GroupNode(nested boundary)$(/f)"
    },
    {
      "type": "modopedia:text",
      "x": 2,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 96,
      "line_height": 9,
      "text": "• Children are filtered by bounds and valid strokes first.\n• Nesting lets projection, emission, and composition operations consume another array."
    },
    {
      "type": "modopedia:text",
      "x": 2,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 96,
      "line_height": 9,
      "text": "$(el:arrays.02)Read input matchers$(/el)"
    }
  ]
